## Context

Storage contract § 4: document deduplication runs before any line is extracted,
because a duplicate extracted twice doubles every count. Planning-time result
(1500): no tier-1 group and no `edition_of` row touches the 115; one title
equals an extracted document's. Tier 2 was not run because a fresh worktree
has no snapshot bytes. 20 of the 115 have an empty `language`, which the
translation rule (one language canonical per pair) needs.

## Work

- Run tiers 1 to 3 over the 115 against all 369 snapshotted documents, where
  the bytes are (padme, or a worktree with `make jetp-data`). Tier 2 is
  normalised extracted text, or a near-duplicate hash of the text layer with
  the same page count.
- Write `same_as`, `edition_of` and `translation_of` rows as candidates in the
  ledger's row shape; accept or reject each by hand. Name the canonical
  document of every cluster.
- Fill the 20 empty `language` values, from the bytes.
- Positive control first: replay the known mirrors already in the registry
  (`idn-cipp-2023` and its CPR mirror) and see the pass find them, so a
  null on the 115 means something.
- Report the list of documents cleared for extraction, per wave of [[1500]].

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Tiers 1 to 3 ran over the 115 with a positive control that fired
- [ ] Every cluster has a canonical document and a decision row; non-canonical members keep their snapshots as citable bytes
- [ ] No `language` is empty among the 115
- [ ] The cleared list per wave is committed and cited by 1502 to 1505
- [ ] `make jetp-ledger-check` and `make check-fast` pass
